  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A transfer tray and a written transfer list can connect book preparation with the pickup desk.\", \"decision\": \"How should a book move between the preparation area and the desk?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nDesk staff send a transfer list for the readers currently waiting, and preparation helpers fill the tray to match it. Transfers follow immediate pickup demand.\nA helper carries the transfer tray at fixed intervals and checks the written list at both ends. Regular rounds connect the two areas without repeated individual requests.\nPreparation helpers fill the transfer tray and send it with a list after a small batch is ready. The desk receives books and their records together in grouped deliveries."
    }
